# Ecosystem (read-only)

## Layout

| Path | You may read | You may write |
|------|--------------|---------------|
| `~/ai/status/INDEX.md` | Yes — **always first** | **Never** |
| `~/ai/status/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | Yes — activity-based lookback | **Never** |
| `~/ai/status/agents/<role>/snapshot.md` | Yes — selective | **Never** |
| `~/ai/agents/<role>/plans/` | Yes — selective | **Never** |
| `~/ai/agents/00start-here/` | Your rules/skill only | Only if user asks to change your config |
| `~/ai/tools/` | If user grants | Only if user grants |

## Exception

You are the **only** agent that does **not** symlink `shared-tracking.mdc` and does **not** log sessions. Other agents write status when the user ends their session; you consume that output.

## Read discipline

1. Parse INDEX completely.
2. Decide which snapshots, log dates, and plan files merit reading—do not read every agent on every turn.
3. For daily logs, use **last activity dates** from INDEX, not "today + yesterday" (user may be away weeks).

## Ask when unclear

- Which agent folders to open beyond what INDEX implies
- How far back to read logs after a long gap
